Environment: evo-flight-lab:sealed, linux/arm64, --network none;
GCC 14.2.0-19 and Clang 19.1.7. Fixture compiled at -std=gnu11 -O0/-O2
with each oracle. EvoCC --emit=asm --target=aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu uses
the original exported sysroot; gcc-14 assembles/links its output.
Each of the five executables exits 0 (observations collected), and prints:
/work/probes filesystem=65735546 getflags=-1 errno=25 flags=0
/tmp filesystem=ef53 getflags=0 errno=0 flags=80000
The two directories are the host-backed FUSE mount and container-local ext4.
The probe creates only a temporary file, reads filesystem/flag metadata and
removes that file; it never sets immutable or append-only flags.
Thus the original chattr immutable failure's first GETFLAGS ioctl is unsupported
by the benchmark filesystem. This is not an EvoCC value mismatch or chattr PASS.
It does not prove immutable SETFLAGS permission or every filesystem feature.

